{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122694","id":4332128487,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAjcI5w","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122694","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122694.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122694.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122694","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122694/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122694/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122694/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/59bc5046f4bdea22af9cdc50cfb1a4591c8065d6","number":122694,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"wayland: Implement wl_fixes v1","user":{"login":"MonterraByte","id":30274651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMjc0NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30274651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte","html_url":"https://github.com/MonterraByte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonterraByte/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This MR uses the `wl_fixes` global to properly destroy the `wl_registry` object. While this is a correctness fix, and doesn't really have a concrete benefit, it's also a preparation for implementing `wl_fixes` v2, which [does fix a real issue](https://blog.vladzahorodnii.com/2026/03/24/addressing-global-removal-race-in-wayland/).\r\n\r\nThe first commit updates the Wayland headers and dynwrappers to 1.24.0. (The protocol XML itself was already updated in #113733.)\r\nThe second commit binds the `wl_fixes` global, and the third one uses it to call `wl_fixes_destroy_registry`.\r\n\r\nUpdating the headers and dynwrappers doesn't seem to increase the runtime version of libwayland-client. I tested this MR in a Debian 13 and a Debian 12 container, and both worked, despite having only Wayland 1.23.1 and 1.21.0, respectively.\r\nThe latter does print a few dlsym errors when so_wrap is used because it lacks some functions from newer versions of libwayland-client, but that should be OK, since we don't actually use them. The entire `wl_fixes` implementation is on the header side and doesn't require any new symbols, so it works even on very old libwayland-client versions.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471795,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE3OTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:thirdpart